    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0504" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114 EW/1–2745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Embassy in the
                        United Kingdom </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-27T12:00:00-04:00">January 27,
                            1945—12 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>683. For Murphy. British Embassy has made available to Department series Foreign
                    Office telegrams regarding proposed Soviet agreements with British and ourselves
                    for treatment of American, British and Soviet prisoners of war and civilians
                    liberated by our respective forces. One British message indicates SHAEF is
                    working out combined British-American text of agreement to be submitted to Big
                    Three meeting. Suggested British text of this agreement is at considerable
                    variance with proposals State, Army, Navy Committee<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d277-f1"/> is proposing to Joint Chiefs of Staff. Please inform
                    American representatives working on SHAEF draft that Department considers it
                    important that before making any commitments on our behalf they await further
                    instructions which it is hoped will be sent through Joint Chiefs on January
                        29.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d277-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeat to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Acting</hi>
                            </item>
                            <item>(E. D[urbrow])</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d277-f1" n="1" xml:id="d277-f1-content">
                <p>The reference is apparently to the State-War-Navy Coordinating Committee
                    (SWNCC).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d277-f2" n="2" xml:id="d277-f2-content">
                <p>The considerations of SWNCC and certain other Washington agencies were
                    subsequently forwarded to Yalta. They are reflected in the telegram of February
                    7 [<hi rendition="#italic">8</hi>], 1945, from Grew to Stettinius, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg697">p. 697</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
